@startuml
title RuleSphere - Runtime Node Artifact Synchronization (UC-20, UC-27)
hide empty description
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EAF6F8
skinparam stateBorderColor #177E8D
skinparam ArrowColor #527183

' Classifier: RuntimeNodeDeploymentSync (COMET State-Dependent Object)
' Target: Single Runtime Node synchronization lifecycle & fleet convergence constraints (FR-DIST-001..005, NFR-CONS-001)

state "Comparing desired and loaded versions" as Compare {
  Compare : entry / inspectDesiredStateAndGeneration()
}

state Match <<choice>>

state "Node Converged" as Converged {
  Converged : entry / markNodeEligible(); reportNodeConverged(generation, version)
}

state "Synchronizing to desired artifact" as Sync {
  state "Fetching artifact" as Fetch {
    Fetch : entry / downloadImmutableArtifact(desiredVersion)
  }
  state "Checking integrity and contracts" as Check {
    Check : entry / verifyChecksum(); validateCompatibility()
  }
  state "Loading into memory" as Load {
    Load : entry / loadInMemoryZeroRestart(); prepareAtomicSnapshot()
  }
  
  [*] --> Fetch
  Fetch --> Check : fetchSucceeded
  Check --> Load : checkSucceeded [checksumValid && contractsCompatible]
}

state "Synchronization failed" as Failed {
  Failed : entry / retainPriorValidArtifact(); emitFailureAlert(); continueServing()
}

' F-04: Initial transition has no trigger or guard per UML 2.5.1
[*] --> Compare : / initRuntimeNodeSync()

Compare --> Match : stateInspected
' F-10: Robust guard requiring matching version, current generation, and verified eligibility
Match --> Converged : [loadedVersion = desiredVersion && loadedGeneration = desiredGeneration && isEligible = true]
Match --> Sync : [loadedVersion != desiredVersion || loadedGeneration != desiredGeneration || !isEligible]

Converged --> Compare : publicationOrRollbackObserved / updateDesiredTarget()
Sync --> Compare : newerDesiredVersionObserved / discardObsoleteTarget()

Load --> Compare : loadSucceeded / reportLoadedState(); recheckDesiredState()

' F-10: FR-DIST-004 fallback policy on failed load: retain prior eligible artifact
Fetch --> Failed : fetchFailed / recordDiagnostics()
Check --> Failed : checkFailed / recordIntegrityMismatch()
Load --> Failed : loadFailed / recordMemoryAllocationError()

Failed --> Compare : retryScheduled / triggerReconciliation()
Failed --> Compare : newerPublicationObserved / updateDesiredTarget()

Converged : observeFleet / exposeDesiredAndLoaded(nodeId, version, generation, true)
Sync : observeFleet / exposeSyncProgress(nodeId, desiredVersion, progress)
Failed : observeFleet / exposeFailureState(nodeId, lastValidVersion, errorDetails)

note right of Converged
  **Fleet Convergence (NFR-CONS-001):**
  Fleet convergence requires 100% of active Runtime nodes
  to reach Node Converged within <=2.0 seconds
  from publication/rollback event emission.
  Zero-restart delivery ensures uninterrupted serving.
end note

note bottom of Failed
  **FR-DIST-004 Serving Invariant:**
  When synchronization fails, the node MUST NOT crash or halt.
  It retains its previously loaded, eligible immutable artifact,
  continues serving unpinned and valid pinned requests,
  and raises an observable alert for operator reconciliation.
end note

legend bottom
  Transition: event [guard] / effect | entry / action
  Classifier: RuntimeNodeDeploymentSync (COMET State-Dependent Object)
  Complies with UML 2.5.1, FR-DIST-001..005, and NFR-CONS-001 (<=2s fleet SLA, FR-DIST-004 safe retain).
endlegend
@enduml
